&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTE 7--COMMON EQUITY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Our long-term debt obligations contain a provision requiring us to maintain a total funded debt to capitalization ratio of 65% or less. This provision imposes a restriction on our ability to transfer funds to WEC Energy Group in the form of cash distributions. As of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;December&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;31, 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;, none of our retained earnings were restricted as a result of this provision. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;We do not believe that this restriction will materially affect our operations or limit any distributions in the foreseeable future.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTE 8--SHORT-TERM DEBT TO PARENT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 5pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;The following table shows our short-term borrowings and their corresponding weighted-average interest rates as of December 31:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
